framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0019:
  description "Bound paid observations before provider dispatch"

problem P1:
  |
    ADR-0007 atomically bounds physical provider attempts for an observation,
    but deliberately leaves token and monetary policy unresolved. The current
    provider adapter sends battle requests without an explicit completion-token
    maximum, records only provider-reported total tokens, and records no reliable
    monetary value for the current xAI path. A stated token or USD ceiling can
    therefore be exceeded or remain unmeasurable even when the attempt ceiling
    works correctly.

premise DRIVER_AUTHORITY:
  |
    A paid Stage observation must not start an outbound provider attempt unless
    the exact run, provider route, model, price snapshot, maximum token exposure
    and maximum monetary exposure are inside the owner-approved envelope.

premise DRIVER_FAIL_CLOSED:
  |
    Missing usage, an unpriced fallback, an unbounded request, a stale price
    snapshot or an exhausted reservation must stop before the next outbound
    attempt. Unknown token or price evidence must never be replaced with zero.

premise DRIVER_COMPATIBILITY:
  |
    The new controls apply only when an explicitly approved observation budget
    is bound. Ordinary battles and observations without the new contract retain
    their existing behavior until a separate adoption decision says otherwise.

evidence E_BUDGET_CURRENT:
  |
    backend/src/llm/provider-accounting.ts reserves one physical provider
    attempt atomically before transport, but its durable run and attempt records
    have no token or monetary reservation fields. ADR-0007 explicitly says a
    separate conservative token and price policy is still required.

evidence E_ADAPTER_CURRENT:
  |
    backend/src/llm/openai-compatible.ts does not set max_tokens or
    max_completion_tokens for battle Chat Completions. Successful attempts pass
    only usage.total_tokens into the ledger and do not calculate a price.

evidence E_LIVE_ROUTE:
  |
    The 2026-09-04 read-only Cloud Run description of the 100-percent production
    revision kshiai-api-00116-doz found LLM_PROVIDER=xai, no explicit provider
    order or model variables, and indirect credential bindings for xAI, OpenAI
    and Venice. At release commit 4d446e4 the resulting default route is
    xai,openai,venice, so an unavailable provider can change the billed model
    during one observation unless the Stage route is frozen.

evidence E_PROVIDER_CONTROLS:
  |
    xAI's official Management API documentation says an API key can have model
    ACLs, QPM and TPM limits; in-flight requests continue when TPM is reached.
    Its billing documentation also describes team-level prepaid credits and
    postpaid spending limits. These are useful defense in depth but do not by
    themselves bind one six-battle application cohort or its already in-flight
    request. Sources: https://docs.x.ai/developers/management-api-guide,
    https://docs.x.ai/developers/rest-api-reference/management/auth, and
    https://docs.x.ai/developers/rest-api-reference/management/billing.

evidence E_PROVIDER_USAGE:
  |
    xAI documents separate prompt_tokens, cached_tokens, completion_tokens and
    total_tokens in Chat Completions usage, and publishes model-specific input,
    cached-input and output prices with higher long-context bands. Sources:
    https://docs.x.ai/developers/advanced-api-usage/prompt-caching/usage-and-pricing
    and https://docs.x.ai/developers/pricing.

premise OPTIONS based_on E_BUDGET_CURRENT, E_ADAPTER_CURRENT, E_PROVIDER_CONTROLS, E_PROVIDER_USAGE:
  |
    Considered options are: keep post-response totals and accept possible
    overspend; rely only on a provider team or key cap; atomically reserve a
    conservative request envelope in the application in addition to provider
    defense in depth; or waive the token and cost requirement. Post-response
    checks cannot prevent the request that crosses the ceiling. Provider-only
    controls are not cohort-scoped and allow in-flight completion. Waiving the
    requirement silently weakens DAF_AUTHORIZE_STAGE.

decision D1 based_on P1, DRIVER_AUTHORITY, OPTIONS:
  |
    Propose an immutable ObservationBudgetPolicyV1 for each approved paid
    cohort. It names the cohort and allowed run count, expiry, exact providers
    and models, price-snapshot digest and effective date, per-request input and
    completion-token envelopes, physical-attempt ceiling, total reserved-token
    ceiling and total reserved-USD ceiling. A run cannot bind or replace a
    policy after its first provider reservation.
  annotation caveat:
    "Proposed; exact Stage values remain a later owner authorization."

decision D2 based_on D1, E_LIVE_ROUTE, DRIVER_FAIL_CLOSED:
  |
    An approved observation uses only the providers and exact model identifiers
    listed in its policy. An inherited provider order, alias that can silently
    retarget, missing model price or fallback outside the list fails before
    transport. Provider-side key ACL, QPM, TPM, prepaid or spending controls are
    independently read back when used, but remain defense in depth rather than
    the application cohort authority.
  annotation caveat:
    "Proposed; no provider key or billing setting change is authorized."

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, E_PROVIDER_USAGE, DRIVER_FAIL_CLOSED:
  |
    Before each physical outbound attempt, the common observation transport
    derives a finite conservative token and charge envelope from the frozen
    request input bound, explicit completion-token maximum, exact model and
    worst applicable price band. It atomically reserves that envelope together
    with the ADR-0007 physical attempt. Transport starts only if all three
    ceilings have room. If a provider-specific token counter cannot prove a
    conservative input bound including protocol overhead, the policy must use
    the model's full documented context limit or reject the request.
  annotation caveat:
    "Proposed; implementation must prove the bound before any real provider call."

decision D4 based_on D3, DRIVER_FAIL_CLOSED:
  |
    Completion records prompt, cached-input, completion, reasoning when
    separately returned, total tokens, exact price-snapshot identity and the
    calculated charge. Missing or contradictory usage fails observation
    acceptance and stops the cohort. Reserved maxima are not released after a
    crash or unknown outcome; conservative over-reservation is preferred to
    unbounded retry.
  annotation caveat:
    "Proposed; accounting evidence remains internal and sanitized."

decision D5 based_on D1, DRIVER_AUTHORITY:
  |
    The Stage observer targets one exact tagged no-traffic Cloud Run revision,
    verifies its digest and compact deployment-override receipt, and executes
    the six frozen battles sequentially. Each slot has one predetermined run
    identity; a stopped or failed slot ends the cohort without replacement.
    The controller never requires the revision to receive production traffic
    and never authorizes Promote.
  annotation caveat:
    "Proposed; Stage release side effects retain their separate authorization."

decision D6 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, DRIVER_COMPATIBILITY:
  |
    Acceptance of this ADR would authorize only local schema, provider-boundary,
    Stage-controller and regression-test implementation. It would not authorize
    a database migration execution, provider or billing mutation, release tag,
    artifact publication, Stage dispatch, provider call, Promote, production
    observation or persisted compact-setting write.
  annotation caveat:
    "Proposed authority boundary; external actions remain separately gated."

pending OWNER_DECISION:
  |
    The product and release owner must accept, revise or reject D1 through D6.
    Generic continuation does not accept this ADR. If accepted, the exact
    provider, model, price snapshot, numerical ceilings, six run identities and
    release artifacts still require the later DAF_AUTHORIZE_STAGE decision.

pending INPUT_BOUND_PROOF:
  |
    Local implementation must demonstrate that its request-input token bound is
    conservative for every allowed provider/model and includes provider-added
    protocol overhead. If this cannot be proved at a practical ceiling, return
    to the owner rather than replacing the hard ceiling with a postflight alert.

pending INTEGRATION_BASE:
  |
    ADR-0019 is allocated after local ADR-0018. Recheck the next free identity
    against verified current main before integration.
